# ========================================
# Templates
# ========================================

> etc/templates

- Holds all templates used in generation of PDF documents using the Aspose library

> etc/templates/DeliveryNoteCyrillic.docx

- The main document for Delivery Notes. This document will reference other documents such as the Header.docx,
  MaterialLogos.docx, BulkItems.docx, and the BagItems.docx templates.

> etc/templates/CollectiveDeliveryNoteCyrillic.docx

- The main document for Collective Delivery Notes. This document references the Header.docx template.


# ========================================
# Templating
# ========================================

## How to create a template
---------------------------

* Create a normal Word 2010 docx file or use an existing one.

* Go to the `Developer` Ribbon and activate "Design Mode".

* Mark a bit of text that should be updated by the processor.

* Select `Rich Text Content Control`. Very broad blue-colored parentheses
 should appear around the text.

* Go to properties.

* Enter a `title` that helps the next person to understand what you want to do

* Enter a `tag` that uses `@`-notation.

* Repeat.


## How to transform a template on the console
---------------------------------------------

* Create the officeTemplate alias an work in the directory 
  `officetemplate-jsf2app-web`

>  alias officetemplate='java -classpath "./build/officetemplate-jsf2app-web/WEB-INF/classes:../lib/Aspose.Words.jdk16.jar:../lib/commons-lang3-3.1.jar" ch.adnovum.officetemplate.jsf2app.console.Program'

* run the alias
   
The command line sample application uses key-value pairs provided in a text
file or on stdin. It supports base64 encoded binary data such as images and
include-documents, as well as references to binary data in the files system.



# ========================================
# The '@'-Notation User Manual
# ========================================

All `Content Controls` whose `tag` starts with an `@` are processed by the
templating engine. After some control-flow (loops, conditions)
transformations, the templating engine will replace the content of a 
`Content Control` with the values provided by your implementation of the 
`DataProvider` class.

The tag should be something like `@path.like` and contain alphanumeric
letters. Using dots to organize your data in an hierarchical manner is
strongly encouraged. For example,

> @person.name
> @person.address1
> @person.address2
> @person.city

## Referencing Values
---------------------

Possible values: 

* If no is provided by your `DataProvider`, the content control is
emptied and removed from the document.

* `TextValue`: Any `Rich Text Content Control` or `Text Content Control`
  tagged with a `@path.like` has its content replaced by the templating engine.

* `ImageValue`: Any `Picture Content Control` tagged with a `@path.like` has
  its content replaced by the templating engine.

* `DocumentValue`: Any `Rich Text Content Control` tagged with a `@include path.like`
  has its content replaced by the templating engine. 


## Conditions
-------------

If the tag of a `Rich Text Content Control` starts with `@if ` or `@if-not`, the control
gets removed if the condition does not evaluate to true. Possible conditions
are

> @if path.like

> @if-not path.like

It is up to the data provider to properly set the "path.like" flag to the appropriate Boolean values.


## Loops
--------

If the tag of a `Rich Text Content Control` starts with `@foreach `, the
contents of the control get repeated `n` times. `n` has to be determined by
the `DataProvider`.

> @foreach person
>
>    @person.name
>    @person.address

will be expanded into this:

>    
>    @person[0].name
>    @person[0].address
>
>    @person[1].name
>    @person[1].address


## Includes
-----------

If the tag of a `Rich Text Content Control` starts with `@include `, then contents
of the control gets removed and replaced with the referenced document. For example,

> @include Header.docx

results in the `Rich Text Content Control` node being replaced by the contents of Header.docx.
In this case, the DataProvider is queried for retrieving the contents of the given
document.


# ========================================
# Testing
# ========================================

In order to make testing easier, the following two adnant commands can be used:

> adnant test-dn-pdf
> adnant test-cdn-pdf

They both use the DeliveryNoteCyrillic.docx and CollectiveDeliveryNoteCyrillic.docx templates resp. and
the src/test/etc/DeliveryNoteCyrillic.properties file for filling in the results. This avoids having to
deploy the template files (they are packaged up as part of the logon-pdf-generator.jar) with every little
change.
